% Presumptions: what is taken to be so when the text is silent.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the kind of *a good* is *a kind*; undefined.
    the fabric construction of *a garment* is *a construction*.
    the fabric of *a garment* is lightweight.

the knowledge base customs presumptions includes:

rule tshirt_fabric with provenance ruling NY N362034,
        confer "To be classifiable as a T-shirt, a garment must be constructed from lightweight, plain jersey or plain interlock fabric":
the fabric of a garment is lightweight
    if the kind of the garment is T-shirt.

rule tshirt_knitted with provenance ruling NY N362034,
        confer "To be classifiable as a T-shirt, a garment must be constructed from lightweight, plain jersey or plain interlock fabric":
the fabric construction of a garment is knitted
    if the kind of the garment is T-shirt.

scenario tee is:
    the kind of item one is T-shirt.
    fabrics expects answers ["the fabric of item one is lightweight"].
    constructions expects answers ["the fabric construction of item one is knitted"].

query fabrics is:
    the fabric of which garment is lightweight.

query constructions is:
    the fabric construction of which garment is which construction.
